<title>USA: NationsBanc to expand leveraged finance unit.</title>
<headline>NationsBanc to expand leveraged finance unit.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-04-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>NationsBanc Capital Markets Inc plans to hire up to a dozen additional investment bankers in its leveraged finance unit within the next three- to six-months, according to NationsBanc officials.</p>
<p>The bank plans plans to hire specialists in leveraged buyouts as well as the media and telecommunications sectors. NationsBanc officials said these areas represent an important and growing part of the bank's current leveraged finance business.</p>
<p>NationsBanc is the fixed-income and investment banking subsidiary of NationsBank Corp, the Charlotte, N.C.-based commercial bank.</p>
<p>((--Douglas Brown, 212-859-1662))</p>
